## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-system cache invalidation strategies across Redis and Memcached with production-grade considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-cache invalidation across backends
- Version stamping and invalidation streams
- Redis Lua atomicity
- Memcached revalidation via version check
- Cache stampede avoidance

## Code Example
```javascript
-- Redis Lua snippet to bump version and emit invalidate
local ver = redis.call('INCR', KEYS[1])
redis.call('XADD', KEYS[2], '*', 'content_id', ARGV[1], 'ver', ver)
return ver
```
```javascript
// Read path for Redis cache
async function readFeed(userId, contentId) {
  const ver = await redis.get(`content:${contentId}:ver`)
  const key = `feed:${userId}:v:${ver}`
  let data = await redis.get(key)
  if (!data) { data = loadFeedFromDB(userId); redis.set(key, JSON.stringify(data), 'EX', 300) }
  return data
}

// Read path for Memcached
async function readFeedMem(userId, contentId) {
  const ver = await redis.get(`content:${contentId}:ver`)
  const key = `feed:${userId}:v:${ver}`
  let data = memcached.get(key)
  if (!data) { data = loadFeedFromDB(userId); memcached.set(key, data, ttl) }
  return data
}
```

